Task 12. Kept only Kaval & April, Shilpa, and Dhan & Christina —
unedited, verbatim, per hard rule 2. Deleted the other five blocks
(Karan & Sonal, Charly & Viola, Shincy, Swati, Druma & Parin).

No image imports became unused: every removed testimonial's photo is
still referenced by /real-weddings/ and/or sitemap-images.xml, so
nothing was deleted there.

Replaced the Trustpilot link under the testimonial grid with
`<a href="#">Read our reviews on Google</a>` and the specified
{/* TODO(owner): replace with Google Business Profile reviews URL */}.

Also fixed a review-schema violation this trim would otherwise cause
(hard rule 7 — did the safe part, flagging it here). app/page.tsx built
the homepage Review + AggregateRating schema from VISIBLE_TESTIMONIALS,
which holds four couples — three no longer visible on the homepage
after this change, one deleted outright. That is the same "schema
without matching visible reviews" problem commit 93c917b and the
layout.tsx FAQ removal were cleaning up. The rendered array is now
exported as HOMEPAGE_TESTIMONIALS and the schema maps over it, so
reviewCount is 3 and matches what the page shows.

OUT OF SCOPE, FLAGGING: a separate "Read all reviews on Trustpilot" CTA
remains in the reviews strip lower on the homepage (~line 806), plus
Trustpilot links in global-footer.tsx, real-weddings/page.tsx and a
sameAs entry in lib/seo.tsx. The brief names only the testimonial-section
link, so I left those. Owner should decide.

Verified: npx tsc --noEmit exit 0.
